speechtext:
The point raised by my hon. friend is taken care of, in my view, in paragraph (a), which reads as follows:
-defining the circumstances and conditions under which the rights of an employee under this part may be waived or the enjoyment thereof postponed;
As I recollect the instances given by my hon. friend, they related to the postponement of the enjoyment of these vacation rights and whether they could be accumulated or enjoyed in the form of additional compensation. I think this could be made possible by the exercise of the authority of paragraph (a) in clause 22.
